---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
import "../../styles/course.css";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="Four checkpoints rather than a weekly meeting: the semester has four moments where something has to leave the room."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    There is no weekly tutorial. The lectures run every week and the work happens
    in your own log; these four sessions exist because each one produces something
    that cannot be produced alone.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first opens your position and seals a record you may not revise. The
    second makes you defend one number out loud before the deadline that depends
    on it. The third takes a rule off you in writing, so that it cannot be
    adjusted after you see how it does. The fourth pools the whole class's
    numbers, which is the one artefact no individual student can make.
  </p>
  <p>
    Bring the <a href={withBase("/records/")}>log</a> to all four.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
